WEBVTT

1
00:00:06.000 --> 00:00:12.074


2
00:00:48.350 --> 00:00:51.975
- [Narrator] Early 1930s,
fascism is on the rise,

3
00:00:51.975 --> 00:00:54.642
and organized crime is born in England.

4
00:00:54.642 --> 00:00:58.975
Two gangs, the Italian Sabinis
and the English White family,

5
00:00:58.975 --> 00:01:01.600
join forces to consolidate
their control of London's

6
00:01:01.600 --> 00:01:05.142
West End and its murky underworld.

7
00:01:05.142 --> 00:01:08.975
In different parts of
town, two as-yet unknowns,

8
00:01:08.975 --> 00:01:11.683
Jack Spot Comer and Billy Hill,

9
00:01:11.683 --> 00:01:15.433
are starting to make
a name for themselves.

10
00:01:15.433 --> 00:01:18.767
This city has never looked so dangerous.

11
00:01:27.558 --> 00:01:30.975
(Muffled lively chatter)

12
00:01:32.808 --> 00:01:36.100
- This Sunday, that pernicious
bastard, Oswald Mosley,

13
00:01:36.100 --> 00:01:38.642
will bring his British Union of Fascists

14
00:01:38.642 --> 00:01:40.517
through the East End!

15
00:01:40.517 --> 00:01:43.558
Through our East End, we're
not gonna let him, are we?

16
00:01:43.558 --> 00:01:44.350
No!
No!

17
00:01:45.558 --> 00:01:47.433
- So, let me ask you a question.

18
00:01:47.433 --> 00:01:51.767
Who here will join me in
protecting our homes, our families,

19
00:01:51.767 --> 00:01:55.475
our livelihood against that
treacherous hate mongering scum?

20
00:01:55.475 --> 00:01:57.642
(Crowd cheers)

21
00:01:57.642 --> 00:01:59.558
- [Narrator] Meet Jack Spot Comer.

22
00:01:59.558 --> 00:02:03.975
Small part Jewish social
crusader, big part agnostic thug.

23
00:02:03.975 --> 00:02:06.350
He's cleaning up in his
local man of White chapel,

24
00:02:06.350 --> 00:02:08.475
and the East End generally.

25
00:02:08.475 --> 00:02:11.225
Nothing's going to stop him
becoming a serious player.

26
00:02:11.225 --> 00:02:13.933
<i>Not even Mosley and his fascists.</i>

27
00:02:15.683 --> 00:02:16.600
- Mr. Comer.

28
00:02:18.517 --> 00:02:20.142
Just as you said.

29
00:02:20.142 --> 00:02:22.433
The top third filled with lead.

30
00:02:22.433 --> 00:02:25.433
I hope you smash those
Blackshirts' brains in.

31
00:02:25.433 --> 00:02:27.392
- [Jack] Very good, Mr. Nelson.

32
00:02:27.392 --> 00:02:28.183
Very good.

33
00:02:29.725 --> 00:02:33.100
(Moody orchestral music)

34
00:04:24.683 --> 00:04:27.183
- For the charge of grievous bodily harm,

35
00:04:27.183 --> 00:04:30.683
inciting public unrest,
and attacking not one,

36
00:04:30.683 --> 00:04:33.183
but several officers of the law,

37
00:04:33.183 --> 00:04:37.100
I hereby sentence you to
six months hard labor.

38
00:04:40.517 --> 00:04:43.017
(Tyres screech)

39
00:04:43.017 --> 00:04:44.892
- [Man] On your toes, Bear!

40
00:04:44.892 --> 00:04:47.017
<i>(Glass smashes)
(alarm rings)</i>

41
00:04:47.017 --> 00:04:49.225
- [Narrator] This is Billy
Hill, a North London boy,

42
00:04:49.225 --> 00:04:51.517
but he don't mind where
his work takes him.

43
00:04:51.517 --> 00:04:53.850
A prolific burglar and a deft thief.

44
00:04:53.850 --> 00:04:56.475
Ambition is definitely not
something he's short of.

45
00:04:56.475 --> 00:04:58.933
(Alarm rings)

46
00:05:02.225 --> 00:05:04.850
<i>(glass smashes)</i>

47
00:05:11.975 --> 00:05:14.267
- [Billy] Thank you, Mrs. Bennett.

48
00:05:14.267 --> 00:05:19.225
(Mrs. Bennett sobs)
(car engine revs)

49
00:05:19.642 --> 00:05:22.392
(tyres screech)

50
00:05:22.392 --> 00:05:25.100
(hushed chatter)

51
00:05:33.558 --> 00:05:35.350
- [Man] Alright, next.

52
00:05:41.392 --> 00:05:43.392
- Mr. Sabini, Mr. White.

53
00:05:44.267 --> 00:05:45.933
Harry.

54
00:05:45.933 --> 00:05:47.725
- It's Mr. White to you.

55
00:05:47.725 --> 00:05:52.267
- There's only one Mr. White
here and that's your father.

56
00:05:52.267 --> 00:05:53.725
- Sit down, Harry.

57
00:05:55.600 --> 00:05:57.392
I said, sit down.

58
00:05:57.392 --> 00:05:59.600
Don't make me tell you twice.

59
00:06:01.892 --> 00:06:03.642
And you can wipe that smirk off your face,

60
00:06:03.642 --> 00:06:05.225
you dirty little toerag.

61
00:06:05.225 --> 00:06:10.100
There's an hierarchy around
here, son, don't you forget it.

62
00:06:12.100 --> 00:06:13.975
Apologise to Mr. White.

63
00:06:18.975 --> 00:06:22.600
- Apologies, Mr. White,
nothing disrespectful meant.

64
00:06:22.600 --> 00:06:23.433
- Prick.

65
00:06:23.433 --> 00:06:24.725
- That's enough!

66
00:06:26.558 --> 00:06:29.308
- Apologies, Mr. Sabini.

67
00:06:29.308 --> 00:06:32.933
- You're becoming quite a regular
round here, ain't ya, son?

68
00:06:32.933 --> 00:06:35.392
Word on the street is, you
knocked off that same jeweller’s

69
00:06:35.392 --> 00:06:38.308
in Hutton Gardens twice in one week.

70
00:06:38.308 --> 00:06:41.100
You fancy yourself a bit, do ya, Billy?

71
00:06:41.100 --> 00:06:43.350
- Just got a sense of humour, that's all.

72
00:06:43.350 --> 00:06:45.017
- Yeah, well that's funny.

73
00:06:45.017 --> 00:06:47.225
What won't be funny is if
you make me laugh today

74
00:06:47.225 --> 00:06:49.808
with the size of your spoils.

75
00:06:49.808 --> 00:06:51.392
From what I gather,

76
00:06:53.975 --> 00:06:56.392
I need at least 50 quid.

77
00:06:56.392 --> 00:07:00.600
- I ain't got 50.
(Harry chuckles)

78
00:07:02.475 --> 00:07:03.267
Here's 80.

79
00:07:10.475 --> 00:07:11.850
- Good boy.

80
00:07:11.850 --> 00:07:12.975
Very good boy.

81
00:07:17.100 --> 00:07:20.975
(Lively soft orchestral music)

82
00:07:22.475 --> 00:07:24.975
(Billy sighs)

83
00:07:37.225 --> 00:07:39.017
- Hello, Billy.

84
00:07:39.017 --> 00:07:40.892
- [Billy] Hello, Aggie.

85
00:07:43.017 --> 00:07:44.892
(Tyres screech)

86
00:07:44.892 --> 00:07:47.267
(car clunks)

87
00:07:48.142 --> 00:07:50.100
(dramatic orchestral music)

88
00:07:50.100 --> 00:07:51.267
- It's the third time we've seen this

89
00:07:51.267 --> 00:07:53.058
and we still don't know how it ends.

90
00:07:53.058 --> 00:07:54.808
- And it's my favourite.
(Aggie chuckles)

91
00:07:54.808 --> 00:07:56.767
- It's my favourite, too.

92
00:07:57.725 --> 00:08:00.433
(Dramatic music)

93
00:08:10.975 --> 00:08:13.350
(doors bang)

94
00:08:30.058 --> 00:08:32.600
(lively music)

95
00:08:39.225 --> 00:08:41.308
- Hey, Jack, good to see ya.

96
00:08:41.308 --> 00:08:42.642
- How you doing?

97
00:08:42.642 --> 00:08:44.725
- Hey, Jack, welcome back.
(Jack laughs)

98
00:08:44.725 --> 00:08:47.642
I'll get you a pint.
- Yeah. (Laughs)

99
00:08:47.642 --> 00:08:50.183
How you doing?
- Good to see ya.

100
00:08:54.225 --> 00:08:55.850
- Moisha.

101
00:08:55.850 --> 00:08:58.183
- Welcome home, how are ya?
- Good.

102
00:08:58.183 --> 00:09:00.975
Sonny. (Chuckles)

103
00:09:04.183 --> 00:09:05.142
- Mr. Comer.

104
00:09:08.933 --> 00:09:10.850
The name's Mulley.

105
00:09:10.850 --> 00:09:11.892
Darky Mulley.

106
00:09:13.142 --> 00:09:16.350
I own four Spielers in Soho
and have vested interests

107
00:09:16.350 --> 00:09:19.058
in every racecourse south of Cheltenham.

108
00:09:19.058 --> 00:09:22.225
I'm not a gangster, Mr Comer,
I'm not even a criminal,

109
00:09:22.225 --> 00:09:24.642
but what I do is not entirely legal,

110
00:09:24.642 --> 00:09:27.308
and for that reason, I
sometimes get some lowlife

111
00:09:27.308 --> 00:09:30.850
and some scum that frequent the property.

112
00:09:30.850 --> 00:09:33.392
Some of them are quite pleasant and fun,

113
00:09:33.392 --> 00:09:35.892
but some of them are not.

114
00:09:35.892 --> 00:09:38.975
I'm looking for an employee
who can handle the latter.

115
00:09:38.975 --> 00:09:41.808
In no uncertain terms,
I'll pay you a decent sum

116
00:09:41.808 --> 00:09:45.642
to take care of that and as
long as you don't kill anyone,

117
00:09:45.642 --> 00:09:46.683
the bobbies will stay off your back,

118
00:09:46.683 --> 00:09:49.767
'cause I'll pay them a decent sum, too.

119
00:09:49.767 --> 00:09:53.392
I'm not looking for a bargain, Mr Comer,

120
00:09:53.392 --> 00:09:56.517
or someone who gets too
big for their boots.

121
00:09:56.517 --> 00:10:00.767
I'm a fair man and I expect
you to do what I ask,

122
00:10:00.767 --> 00:10:03.683
and I expect you to do
it without any trouble.

123
00:10:03.683 --> 00:10:06.725
Now, if you can do this,
we'll get on handsomely.

124
00:10:06.725 --> 00:10:09.433
If you can't, I shall
thank you for your time,

125
00:10:09.433 --> 00:10:11.933
and I shall find someone else.

126
00:10:16.725 --> 00:10:19.142
- (Laughs) Alright, who
invented copper wire?

127
00:10:19.142 --> 00:10:20.183
- Who?

128
00:10:20.183 --> 00:10:22.350
- Two kikes fighting over a farthing.

129
00:10:22.350 --> 00:10:24.642
(Men laugh)

130
00:10:27.225 --> 00:10:29.392
Why do Jews get circumcised?

131
00:10:29.392 --> 00:10:30.225
- [Man] Why is that?

132
00:10:30.225 --> 00:10:31.767
- [Joker] 'Cause Jew
birds won't touch nothing,

133
00:10:31.767 --> 00:10:35.558
unless there's 20 % off!
(Men laugh)

134
00:10:35.558 --> 00:10:37.100
- Comedian, are ya?

135
00:10:40.600 --> 00:10:44.058
What's the definition of a Jewish dilemma?

136
00:10:46.517 --> 00:10:49.517
Free pork. (Laughs)

137
00:10:50.517 --> 00:10:52.808
(men laugh)

138
00:10:57.808 --> 00:10:59.225
I got tonnes of these.

139
00:10:59.225 --> 00:11:00.892
This is one of my favorites.

140
00:11:00.892 --> 00:11:03.392
What happens when a
Jew walks into the wall

141
00:11:03.392 --> 00:11:04.808
with an erection?

142
00:11:04.808 --> 00:11:05.767
- What?

143
00:11:05.767 --> 00:11:07.808
- He breaks his nose. (Laughs)

144
00:11:07.808 --> 00:11:08.850
<i>(glass smashes)</i>

145
00:11:08.850 --> 00:11:11.433
Got another one, a Jew boy
walks into his dad and says,

146
00:11:11.433 --> 00:11:15.558
"Give me 20 quid." (Laughs)

147
00:11:15.558 --> 00:11:18.350
(spectators yell)

148
00:11:21.475 --> 00:11:24.142
(fast rumbling)

149
00:11:25.392 --> 00:11:28.142
(crowd cheering)

150
00:11:38.975 --> 00:11:41.183
<i>- Oh, useless bloody horse!</i>

151
00:11:51.892 --> 00:11:53.308
That was very passionate.

152
00:11:53.308 --> 00:11:55.433
- Mom says you're a bad influence on me.

153
00:11:55.433 --> 00:11:57.142
- Wish I was a worse influence on ya.

154
00:11:57.142 --> 00:11:59.058
- So do I.
- Do ya?

155
00:11:59.058 --> 00:12:00.600
- Well, yeah.

156
00:12:00.600 --> 00:12:05.142
But don't wanna get a bad
name for myself, do I?

157
00:12:05.142 --> 00:12:06.183
- Aggie Hill.

158
00:12:07.225 --> 00:12:09.975
What'd you think of that?

159
00:12:09.975 --> 00:12:12.850
- Now you're teasing me.
- No, I ain't.

160
00:12:12.850 --> 00:12:16.017
You wouldn't get a bad name
for yourself then, would ya?

161
00:12:16.017 --> 00:12:19.017
- I don't like it when you tease me.

162
00:12:19.017 --> 00:12:21.350
- I'm not teasing.

163
00:12:21.350 --> 00:12:22.808
What do you think?

164
00:12:26.558 --> 00:12:28.475
- Let's try win some money, come on.

165
00:12:28.475 --> 00:12:30.100
- That's my girl.

166
00:12:30.100 --> 00:12:32.225
- [Bookie] Come on, ladies
and gentlemen, come on!

167
00:12:32.225 --> 00:12:34.933
10 pound, Win Rider, five to one!

168
00:12:39.350 --> 00:12:43.642
Low Ranger at four to one,
Win Rider at five to one.

169
00:12:45.100 --> 00:12:47.975
(Group chattering)

170
00:13:18.808 --> 00:13:21.683
(footsteps)

171
00:13:21.683 --> 00:13:23.933
- [Jack] Get out, out!

172
00:13:23.933 --> 00:13:24.725
Out.

173
00:13:28.475 --> 00:13:30.600
(Banging)

174
00:13:38.558 --> 00:13:39.350
Mr May?

175
00:13:40.433 --> 00:13:42.350
I know you're in there.

176
00:13:43.517 --> 00:13:47.017
You come out now and I won't hurt ya.

177
00:13:47.017 --> 00:13:51.683
You can't go around abusing
Mr Mulley’s pitch like that.

178
00:14:01.183 --> 00:14:03.642
Don't make me do this, Mr May.

179
00:14:10.308 --> 00:14:13.642
(Grunts)
(Mall groans)

180
00:14:13.642 --> 00:14:17.308
- [Man] Whoa, whoa, whoa,
drop the knife, pal.

181
00:14:17.308 --> 00:14:18.850
Stand up.

182
00:14:18.850 --> 00:14:19.642
Slowly.

183
00:14:21.267 --> 00:14:23.808
(Knife clanks)

184
00:14:25.683 --> 00:14:28.808
(laughing)
(upbeat folk music)

185
00:14:28.808 --> 00:14:30.558
- Only a mug would shoot someone,

186
00:14:30.558 --> 00:14:32.600
'cause if you kill 'em,
that's the death penalty.

187
00:14:32.600 --> 00:14:33.808
Understand?

188
00:14:33.808 --> 00:14:36.183
Each time you on about
the Whites or the Sabinis,

189
00:14:36.183 --> 00:14:38.100
and trust me, you do,

190
00:14:38.100 --> 00:14:41.267
I ain't stupid, so once
I worked that one out,

191
00:14:41.267 --> 00:14:44.975
I knew I was just gonna get a beating.

192
00:14:44.975 --> 00:14:47.475
(Woman pants)

193
00:14:49.808 --> 00:14:52.267
(woman moans)

194
00:14:59.683 --> 00:15:01.183
- Jack.

195
00:15:01.183 --> 00:15:02.933
Elephant Dave's here.

196
00:15:04.225 --> 00:15:05.517
- Alright, Dave?

197
00:15:06.683 --> 00:15:07.475
- Jack.

198
00:15:09.350 --> 00:15:11.600
Just let me finish up and
I'll be right with ya.

199
00:15:11.600 --> 00:15:13.642
- Right you are.

200
00:15:13.642 --> 00:15:16.100
(Woman moans)

201
00:15:24.017 --> 00:15:26.142
- Thank you for coming, and
thank you for sharing my

202
00:15:26.142 --> 00:15:29.017
enthusiasm for the London
County and Westminster job,

203
00:15:29.017 --> 00:15:32.308
which I believe will
be our biggest to date.

204
00:15:32.308 --> 00:15:33.892
Most of you know each other,

205
00:15:33.892 --> 00:15:36.683
but as we've got a few new
faces and as is customary,

206
00:15:36.683 --> 00:15:39.225
I'm gonna start by making
a few introductions.

207
00:15:39.225 --> 00:15:42.642
Elephant Dave, he's our
resident cat burglar.

208
00:15:42.642 --> 00:15:43.975
He's already done his job,

209
00:15:43.975 --> 00:15:46.642
hence his replica key to the front door.

210
00:15:46.642 --> 00:15:50.892
Billy Sparks and Mark Bear,
they're alarm specialists.

211
00:15:50.892 --> 00:15:53.142
Mr Russell fit the alarm system.

212
00:15:53.142 --> 00:15:55.975
Our confidence man on the inside as such.

213
00:15:55.975 --> 00:15:58.517
Big Bob, Grinning Mike and Easy Alan

214
00:15:58.517 --> 00:16:01.600
will break the safes,
hopefully in minutes.

215
00:16:01.600 --> 00:16:05.058
Jaguar Ken, Motor Mike,
and North Street Ronnie

216
00:16:05.058 --> 00:16:10.017
will nick our getaway vehicles
and drive us all to safety.

217
00:16:10.142 --> 00:16:12.517
- We sure it was Spot?

218
00:16:12.517 --> 00:16:16.642
- I've had it from two
reliable faces, it was him.

219
00:16:18.142 --> 00:16:20.767
(Alarm blaring)

220
00:16:26.017 --> 00:16:28.892
(car horn blaring)

221
00:16:36.142 --> 00:16:39.017
(grunting in pain)

222
00:16:48.017 --> 00:16:50.808
- William Hill, your
frequency in these courts

223
00:16:50.808 --> 00:16:54.725
is a national disgrace, and
seeing as you are unwilling

224
00:16:54.725 --> 00:16:57.350
to name your accomplices, I see no choice

225
00:16:57.350 --> 00:17:01.308
but to sentence you to
two years penal servitude.

226
00:17:01.308 --> 00:17:02.600
(Sobbing quietly)

227
00:17:02.600 --> 00:17:03.767
Take him down.

228
00:17:15.225 --> 00:17:20.183
(Murmuring and chattering)
(smooth jazz music)

229
00:17:28.642 --> 00:17:33.600
Gotta build a bridge to you

230
00:17:33.933 --> 00:17:38.892
Gotta take some time to do

231
00:17:39.142 --> 00:17:43.933
I have got to make a start

232
00:17:43.933 --> 00:17:46.392
And build it straight

233
00:17:46.392 --> 00:17:50.100
Straight to your heart ♪

234
00:17:50.100 --> 00:17:55.058
Gotta wait eternally

235
00:17:55.725 --> 00:18:00.642
Might take eternity

236
00:18:00.683 --> 00:18:05.350
But while we're still apart ♪

237
00:18:05.350 --> 00:18:08.100
I'll build it straight ♪

238
00:18:08.100 --> 00:18:11.058
Straight to your heart ♪

239
00:18:11.058 --> 00:18:16.058
I will build it night and day

240
00:18:16.267 --> 00:18:18.642
Never resting

241
00:18:18.642 --> 00:18:19.892
(gun clicking)

242
00:18:19.892 --> 00:18:23.183
(man screaming in pain)

243
00:18:27.600 --> 00:18:30.933
(screaming in pain)

244
00:18:30.933 --> 00:18:32.433
- Shut up!

245
00:18:32.433 --> 00:18:34.433
Shut up, shut up!

246
00:18:34.433 --> 00:18:36.225
- Please, please Jack.

247
00:18:37.725 --> 00:18:39.975
- Please, please Jack, please Jack.

248
00:18:39.975 --> 00:18:42.350
You sound like a little girl.

249
00:18:46.017 --> 00:18:48.475
Who put you up to this?

250
00:18:48.475 --> 00:18:50.392
Who put you up to this?

251
00:18:54.017 --> 00:18:54.808
No?

252
00:19:03.183 --> 00:19:04.225
Unbelievable,

253
00:19:06.350 --> 00:19:08.058
Unbelievable.

254
00:19:08.058 --> 00:19:08.892
- What?

255
00:19:14.600 --> 00:19:15.475
Bloody hell.

256
00:19:22.725 --> 00:19:26.225
Let's say goodbye with a smile dear

257
00:19:26.225 --> 00:19:31.183
Just for a while dear we must part ♪

258
00:19:33.350 --> 00:19:37.308
Don't let this parting upset you

259
00:19:37.308 --> 00:19:42.308
I'll not forget you sweetheart

260
00:19:46.183 --> 00:19:51.142
We'll meet again don't
know where, don't know when

261
