00:40:25.017 --> 00:40:26.767
- A da da da dah, yes
you do, pay me the money.

530
00:40:26.767 --> 00:40:28.933
- But I don't have any..
- Pay me the money,

531
00:40:28.933 --> 00:40:30.683
pay me the money
- Oi!

532
00:40:33.017 --> 00:40:35.600
Lay off him, he's mine.

533
00:40:35.600 --> 00:40:36.642
- Not anymore

534
00:40:38.142 --> 00:40:41.767
(loudspeaker announcements)

535
00:40:56.100 --> 00:40:59.225
- [Billy] Dear Mr Comer,
my name is Billy Hill

536
00:40:59.225 --> 00:41:01.642
and I come out of Camden originally

537
00:41:01.642 --> 00:41:04.767
but I'm writing this letter
to you from Wandsworth nick.

538
00:41:04.767 --> 00:41:07.850
I won't lie, it's not the
first time I've been inside

539
00:41:07.850 --> 00:41:09.808
but it will definitely be the last.

540
00:41:09.808 --> 00:41:13.142
And believe you me, I'm a man of my word.

541
00:41:13.142 --> 00:41:16.308
I come from a large family
where blagging is in our blood.

542
00:41:16.308 --> 00:41:19.267
And so is honor, loyalty and respect

543
00:41:20.475 --> 00:41:22.517
and a need for constant juggling'.

544
00:41:22.517 --> 00:41:24.142
I'm doubting you know who I am.

545
00:41:24.142 --> 00:41:26.975
I very well know who you are,
as I've been a frequenter

546
00:41:26.975 --> 00:41:28.892
at Boots for quite some time now.

547
00:41:28.892 --> 00:41:31.100
I especially like the
house band you introduced

548
00:41:31.100 --> 00:41:33.350
after you took over from the Whites.

549
00:41:33.350 --> 00:41:35.517
Anyway, I've been doin' a lot of thinking

550
00:41:35.517 --> 00:41:36.975
since I've been inside

551
00:41:36.975 --> 00:41:38.225
and I know you Sonny and Moisha

552
00:41:38.225 --> 00:41:39.642
as your loyal and trusted men.

553
00:41:39.642 --> 00:41:41.433
I've even spoken to Moisha a few times

554
00:41:41.433 --> 00:41:43.433
and he's as solid as they come

555
00:41:43.433 --> 00:41:47.558
but, I'd like to offer
you my services, Mr Comer

556
00:41:47.558 --> 00:41:48.683
and I don't say this lightly

557
00:41:48.683 --> 00:41:51.308
as I've never wanted to
work for anyone before.

558
00:41:51.308 --> 00:41:53.767
You're different though, you're smart,

559
00:41:53.767 --> 00:41:56.517
you're forward-thinking
and you're fearless

560
00:41:56.517 --> 00:41:58.017
and I'd like to think our combined skills

561
00:41:58.100 --> 00:42:01.100
can be a dynamic and lethal combination.

562
00:42:01.100 --> 00:42:03.100
If you're at all interested
in finding out more

563
00:42:03.100 --> 00:42:05.017
than what I can put down on paper,

564
00:42:05.017 --> 00:42:08.183
you know where I am and I
hope to hear from you soon.

565
00:42:08.183 --> 00:42:10.475
Yours sincerely, Billy Hill.

566
00:42:13.475 --> 00:42:15.975
- [Man] Hello Jessie, how are you?

567
00:42:15.975 --> 00:42:18.683
- [Jack] I'd like you to
meet my friend, Billy Hill.

568
00:42:18.683 --> 00:42:21.100
- [Man] Hello mate, how good to see you.

569
00:42:21.100 --> 00:42:23.392
- [Jack] Good to see you John

570
00:42:25.142 --> 00:42:26.642
Two Jack bosses please Alex.

571
00:42:26.642 --> 00:42:27.892
- [Barman] Right away Mr Comer.

572
00:42:27.892 --> 00:42:32.850
- They've even named a drink
after me (both laughing)

573
00:42:33.433 --> 00:42:34.225
- Like it?

574
00:42:35.183 --> 00:42:36.183
- Very much.

575
00:42:37.100 --> 00:42:38.433
- This is the high life Billy

576
00:42:38.433 --> 00:42:40.642
and don't let anybody tell you
it isn't bloody marvelous,

577
00:42:40.642 --> 00:42:42.683
'cause it bloody well is.

578
00:42:44.183 --> 00:42:46.725
(Smooth music)

579
00:42:49.558 --> 00:42:52.350
- Why'd you wanna work for me then?

580
00:42:52.350 --> 00:42:53.808
- Well Mr Comer.

581
00:42:53.808 --> 00:42:54.933
- Call me Jack

582
00:42:54.933 --> 00:42:55.767
(menacing music)

583
00:42:55.767 --> 00:42:58.642
- Well Jack, I admire you see,

584
00:42:58.642 --> 00:43:00.850
what you done with the
horses and the spiels.

585
00:43:00.850 --> 00:43:02.642
How you took on the Whites.

586
00:43:02.642 --> 00:43:04.808
Ain't a man who can touch you today.

587
00:43:04.808 --> 00:43:07.350
Well, I blackmailed lives see,

588
00:43:07.350 --> 00:43:09.600
not afraid of hard work I'm not.

589
00:43:09.600 --> 00:43:12.433
Just don't fancy going back
to that khazi you know?

590
00:43:12.433 --> 00:43:14.892
I wanna go steady as such.

591
00:43:14.892 --> 00:43:17.267
Work with the master
of all things criminal.

592
00:43:17.267 --> 00:43:19.642
Hope some of your success rubs off on me,

593
00:43:19.642 --> 00:43:22.808
some of your charm, some of
your organisational skills.

594
00:43:22.808 --> 00:43:24.933
- Not looking for ambitious men Billy,

595
00:43:24.933 --> 00:43:26.517
I'm looking for men who know their place.

596
00:43:26.600 --> 00:43:27.725
Last thing I want is a man who reckons

597
00:43:27.725 --> 00:43:29.767
he knows more than what I do.

598
00:43:29.767 --> 00:43:32.308
- You're the boss Jack, no argument there.

599
00:43:32.308 --> 00:43:33.642
- Handle yourself can ya?

600
00:43:33.642 --> 00:43:35.058
- I reckon so.

601
00:43:35.058 --> 00:43:36.267
Don't look for a fight.

602
00:43:36.267 --> 00:43:38.142
I won't run away from one neither.

603
00:43:38.142 --> 00:43:39.100
- Got a crew?

604
00:43:39.100 --> 00:43:39.933
- Yeah.

605
00:43:39.933 --> 00:43:41.517
Three blokes I trust with me life.

606
00:43:41.517 --> 00:43:43.517
One inside, two on the out.

607
00:43:43.517 --> 00:43:45.058
- Why what hours you keep?

608
00:43:45.058 --> 00:43:47.892
- All I wanna do is graft.

609
00:43:47.892 --> 00:43:49.308
- What about girlfriends?

610
00:43:49.308 --> 00:43:50.767
- I ain't married,

611
00:43:53.767 --> 00:43:54.808
well kind of.

612
00:43:57.808 --> 00:43:59.392
- Like anyone here?

613
00:44:02.308 --> 00:44:05.183
(Group chattering)

614
00:44:11.642 --> 00:44:14.600
- Only the best for Mr
Comer's special friend.

615
00:44:14.600 --> 00:44:17.058
I just hope you can handle her Mr Hill.

616
00:44:17.058 --> 00:44:21.017
The key's in the box on the bedside table.

617
00:44:21.017 --> 00:44:23.683
(Woman moaning)

618
00:44:24.850 --> 00:44:27.808
(suspenseful music)

619
00:44:42.850 --> 00:44:45.308
(door closes)

620
00:45:02.267 --> 00:45:06.058
(woman moaning in other room)

621
00:45:24.850 --> 00:45:27.267
- That says a lot about you Mr Hill.

622
00:45:27.267 --> 00:45:30.225
Most men never undo my hands.

623
00:45:30.225 --> 00:45:32.392
- Suppose I ain't most men.

624
00:45:32.392 --> 00:45:34.933
- I'll tell you in the morning.

625
00:45:39.392 --> 00:45:42.058
Nervous little kitten aren't ya?

626
00:45:43.100 --> 00:45:46.142
(Uptempo jazz music)

627
00:46:05.683 --> 00:46:06.975
- I'm topped, I've got
almost every racecourse

628
00:46:06.975 --> 00:46:08.558
in the south of England.

629
00:46:08.558 --> 00:46:11.308
Ascot, Kempton, Ally Pally Brighton.

630
00:46:11.350 --> 00:46:13.642
I take a cut of everything
through the bookmakers

631
00:46:13.642 --> 00:46:15.642
right on down to the
ice-cream concessions.

632
00:46:15.642 --> 00:46:17.933
Average profit on the day is 5000.

633
00:46:17.933 --> 00:46:20.600
On Derby Day, we cleared 20,000.

634
00:46:20.600 --> 00:46:23.808
- You're making a bloody mint ain't ya?

635
00:46:25.808 --> 00:46:27.350
- Hi Albert.

636
00:46:27.350 --> 00:46:29.183
